BSP-Yocto-TISDK-AM64x-ALPHA2                    2022-10-04
==========================================================

- Linux TI vendor kernel v5.10.120 (based on TI tag 08.04.01.002)
- U-Boot v2021.01 (based on TI tag 08.03.00.005)
- Yocto 3.1.12 (dunfell, based on TI CoreSDK 08.03.00.005)

NOTE:
This is an ALPHA release and has not been tested for full functionality. It is
possible that some features are not working or stable. This release will NOT
be supported after the first full BSP release.


Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------

- tisdk-default-image:
  * phyboard-electra-am64xx-1


Build Environment:
------------------

- Ubuntu 18.04 64-bit


Changes since ALPHA1:
---------------------

- New Features:
  * Support for device tree overlay
    - UART3 + SPI1 via k3-am64-phyboard-electra-x27-uart3-spi1.dtbo
  * Support for Realtak R8169 PCIe card
  * Update device trees to newer Carrier Board and SoM revision
    (PCM-072.A1, PBA-C-25.A1)
  * New memory testing tools for TI image (memtester & stressapptest)

- Fixes:
  * u-boot environment is now stored on boot device


Known Issues:
-------------

- OSPI Boot is failing
- Having identical wic image flashed on eMMC and inserted SD card
  leads to a boot failure due to identical partition UUIDs
